# Conformance probe pack for items of variable size on the `bits` wire (spec
# 0.7, rulings 2 and 4 of 0.7). Public. No kinds. One byte per word, least
# significant bit first.
#
#   byte 0      number of items; also mapped as probe.n
#   then        one item per count:
#     byte 0      qty
#     byte 1      number of subs
#     byte 2...   one byte per sub
#
# `item 24`: an item with no sub or one sub is three bytes. The nested group is
# counted by a locator, is the last thing in its item and may run past the 24
# bits: an item with three subs is five bytes, and the next item starts where
# it ends. The count of items has no `field` of its own and is written over
# probe.n, which is mapped on the same bits.
format     conformance-groups-bits-var
version    0.7.0
distribution public
source  "goat-transformers spec/engine-spec.md (synthetic probe format, no external standard)"
uses       probe
wire       bits
word_bytes 1
field   probe.n  0:0:8  uint
group   probe.items  0:8  item 24  count 0:0:8
  field   probe.qty  0:0:8  uint
  group   probe.subs  0:16  item 8  count 0:8:8
    field  probe.val  0:0:8  uint
  end
end
